A||N||8||foulplayer||Strange Vibration||||1||
Z||000000||foulplayer||12-08-2001||09:12 PM||||I have a '84 Fiero SE V6. When driving on express way, the car just vibrating at an ungodly pase. I have bought all new tires, next going to buy a new axel. <P>Does anyone else know what could cause the vibration?<P>------------------<BR>"Speed.... A Way Of Life."  <BR>--Foulplayer||||reg||1
Z||000001||ejayerik||12-08-2001||09:15 PM||||Try your alignment? Perhaps it is the barrings. It could be the brake calipers. It could be any number of things. Push the front tires around to see if you get some play. Also check the suspension for leaks and wear. Check all of the bushings and look for rub marks.||||reg||1
Z||000002||foulplayer||12-08-2001||09:17 PM||||Forgot to say, I also got an alignment. Which still didnt help. <P>------------------<BR>"Speed.... A Way Of Life."  <BR>--Foulplayer||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mach10||12-08-2001||09:18 PM||||New tires? BALANCING!!! If they've been done, tell 'em that the car is shaking like an absolute bastard. It's possible that a weight came off, or wasn't put on, or whatever. All it takes is to pull the wheel and throw it on the balancer to check  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000004||watts||12-09-2001||12:36 PM||||What speed does the vibration start at?<P>Where (if ever) does it end?<P>Bring it up to the speed it vibrates at, go a litle faster, then toss in neutral and let the engine come down to idle.  Is the vibration still there?<P>How did you manage to con GM into building you an' 84 with a V6?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Speedyfiero||12-09-2001||12:41 PM||||I just bought the '84 with the V6 in it that way from someone. The cars interior is like brand new, the motor is strong, all except for the vibration. It happens when I hit around 55mph then it gets worse the faster i go.||||reg||1
Z||000006||dourain86gt||12-13-2001||02:08 AM||||I have the same problem and I have an 86 Gt I was hoping it would go away with new tires and aligment, but now that you tell me this I am not sure how to fix it?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Blacktree||12-13-2001||05:53 AM||||If it's a wheel vibration (bad alignment, unbalanced wheel, or warped brake disc) the vibration will follow a harmonic pattern. In other words, as you're driving down the road the vibration will get stronger and weaker and stronger and weaker in a predictable pattern. Try to feel if the car is vibrating up-and-down or side-to-side, and if it's coming from the front or rear. <P>If it's a driveline problem, the vibration will get worse and worse the faster you go. And it usually won't follow a harmonic pattern... it'll just be constant.<P>Another thing... once when I bought new tires for my 86 Fiero, they put a defective tire on my car. It had a bubble in the tread. It made the car shake so bad I thought it was going to fall apart.<p>[This message has been edited by Blacktree (edited 12-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||87fastback||12-13-2001||01:55 PM||||Blacktree is correct!  It is an out of balance wheel, wether it be a seperated belt in the tire (it CAN happen on a brand new tire - don't just assume it is ok since it is new), or like Blacktree said a weight kicked off the wheel.  Harmonic vibration that shake the steering wheel when driving down the road and get increasingly worse as speed increases is wheel/tire related!<P>I just spent a BUNCH of time on this issue with my 87 Fastback and it was a bunch of fix-a-flat in the tire.  Cleaned it out and viration gone!<P>Do yourself a favor and go back to the shop and insist they rebalance the tires and check the runout on each.||||reg||1
